34, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1707681\"><a href=\"/opinion/1707681/porter-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Porter v. State\">564 So. 2d 1060</a></span>; No. 90-6445, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9480447\"><a href=\"/opinion/543140/charles-silagy-cross-appellant-v-howard-peters-iii-warden-pontiac/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Charles Silagy, Cross-Appellant v. Howard Peters, Iii,...\">905 F. 2d 986</a></span>; No. 90-6468, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"2284545\"><a href=\"/opinion/2284545/gilliam-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gilliam v. State\">320 Md. 637</a></span>, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"2284545\"><a href=\"/opinion/2284545/gilliam-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gilliam v. State\">579 A. 2d 744</a></span>; No. 90-6480, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"2369355\"><a href=\"/opinion/2369355/state-v-reese/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State v. Reese\">795 S. W. 2d 69</a></span>; No. 90-6663, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9883322\"><a href=\"/opinion/1233910/people-v-ramirez/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: People v. Ramirez\">50 Cal. 3d 1158</a></span>, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9883322\"><a href=\"/opinion/1233910/people-v-ramirez/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: People v. Ramirez\">791 P. 2d 965</a></span>; No. 90-6668, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1262655\"><a href=\"/opinion/1262655/state-v-robinson/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State v. Robinson\">165 Ariz. 51</a></span>, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1262655\"><a href=\"/opinion/1262655/state-v-robinson/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State v. Robinson\">796 P. 2d 853</a></span>.</p>\n</opinion>"},{"id":9100451,"type":"dissent","typeCode":"040dissent","perCuriam":false,"author":"Marshall","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":571,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"dissent\">\n<author id=\"b1076-14\">Justice Marshall,</author>\n<p id=\"AvvS\">dissenting.</p>\n<p id=\"b1076-15\">Adhering to my view that the death penalty is in all circumstances cruel and unusual punishment prohibited by the Eighth and Fourteenth Amendments, <em>Gregg </em>v. <em>Georgia, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9426555\"><a href=\"/opinion/109532/gregg-v-georgia/#231\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gregg v. Georgia\">428 U. S. 153, 231</a></span> (1976), I would grant certiorari and vacate the death sentences in these cases.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}